From: Jason Gross <jason@theorem.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] mes/arm: correct SYS_getdents64 syscall number (0xdc -> 0xd9)

include/linux/arm/syscall.h defined SYS_getdents64 as 0xdc (220) -- the x86
value, copied onto the ARM table. On ARM EABI, syscall 220 is madvise;
getdents64 is 217 (0xd9). The mes libc getdents() (lib/linux/getdents.c,
also inlined in libc.c) prefers SYS_getdents64 whenever it is defined, so on
arm it invoked madvise(dirfd, buffer, nbytes) -> EINVAL. readdir() therefore
left errno=EINVAL after end-of-directory, and GNU make (which checks errno
after its readdir loop) aborted every build with

    make: *** INTERNAL: readdir: error 22

before compiling anything. Cross-checked against the musl arch/arm syscall
table: getdents64 is the sole number that disagrees.
---
--- a/include/linux/arm/syscall.h
+++ b/include/linux/arm/syscall.h
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@
 #define SYS_lstat64    0xc4
 #define SYS_fstat64    0xc5
 #define SYS_fcntl64    0xdd
-#define SYS_getdents64 0xdc
+#define SYS_getdents64 0xd9
 
 #undef SYS_stat
 #define SYS_stat SYS_stat64
